# SRG-APP-000118-WSR-000068  -  CAT II
# Web server log files must only be accessible by privileged users.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000118-WSR-000068
group:           V-206368
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000162
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Splunk Web's access and service records are reachable through the product
                 only by way of the internal indexes, so the application's share is that
                 the general-purpose roles are not granted search of those indexes.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [role_user] srchIndexesAllowed matches tls1\.2
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*ssl3
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.0
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.1
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] srchIndexesAllowed matches tls1\.2
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*ssl3
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.0
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] srchIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|,)[[:space:]]*tls1\.1

external:        File permissions on the log directory holding web_access.log and
                 web_service.log - SPLK-CL-000190 implements this with splunk-user
                 ownership and mode 700 at the operating system layer
external:        Which roles the organization treats as privileged for web server log
                 review

citation:        Three corrections. not_in *|_* carries the same wildcard inversion
                 documented on SRG-APP-000118-AU-000100 and is replaced.
                 srchIndexesDisallowed present is removed because the setting has no
                 default (authorize.conf.spec:297-307) and no shipped role sets it, so the
                 condition marked a stock, correctly scoped install as a finding - and the
                 deny-list is not the only way to express the boundary, since the
                 allow-list already excludes internal indexes. web.conf log.access_file
                 non_empty is removed as vacuous (web.conf.spec:871-874 supplies the
                 default) and because protecting the file itself is the operating system
                 permission that SPLK-CL-000190 sets, now stated as an external dependency
                 instead of being tested as though Splunk configured it.
finding:         The role_user or role_power definition grants search of the internal
                 indexes that carry the Splunk Web access and service records, so those
                 records are readable by unprivileged accounts.
